@startuml RawBin Sprint 2 — Challenge-Response Auth Flow
!theme plain
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title SSH Challenge-Response Authentication (T12)

actor "User" as U
participant "Browser\n(RawBinClient)" as C
participant "Server\n(server.ts)" as S
participant "UserKeys.ts" as K
database "data/users/\n<token>/.ssh/" as SSH

== Returning User — Enrolled Device ==

C -> S : WebSocket connect
S -> S : challenge = crypto.randomBytes(32).hex()
S -> C : welcome { clientId, challenge }

note over C : check localStorage for\nrawbin-device-privateKey

alt Has device keys (enrolled)
  C -> C : PEM → DER (strip headers, base64 decode)
  C -> C : crypto.subtle.importKey('pkcs8', der, RSA)
  C -> C : challengeBytes = hex decode challenge
  C -> C : signature = crypto.subtle.sign(\n  'RSASSA-PKCS1-v1_5', key, challengeBytes)
  C -> C : signedChallenge = btoa(signature)

  C -> S : DEVICE_AUTH {\n  devicePublicKey: localStorage pubKey,\n  signedChallenge: base64\n}

  S -> K : verifyChallenge(token, pubKey, challenge, sig)
  K -> SSH : read authorized_keys
  SSH -> K : [key1, key2, ...]

  alt pubKey in authorized_keys
    K -> K : crypto.verify('sha256',\n  challengeBuffer, pubKey, sigBuffer)

    alt Signature valid
      K -> S : true
      S -> S : client.authenticated = true
      S -> S : client.authMethod = 'device-key'
      S -> S : client.challenge = '' (consumed)
      S -> C : DEVICE_AUTH_OK
      note over C #LightGreen : authenticated via device key

    else Signature invalid
      K -> S : false
      S -> C : DEVICE_AUTH_FAILED { reason: "Invalid signature" }
      note over C : fall back to token auth
    end

  else pubKey NOT in authorized_keys
    K -> S : false
    S -> C : DEVICE_AUTH_FAILED { reason: "Invalid signature" }
  end

  == Always: Token IDENTIFY (for profile data) ==

  C -> S : IDENTIFY { playerToken, deviceId, name }
  S -> C : PROFILE { profile, connectedDeviceIds }

else No device keys (new device or not enrolled)

  == Token-only path (backward compatible) ==

  C -> S : IDENTIFY { playerToken, deviceId, name }
  S -> S : client.authMethod = 'token'
  S -> C : PROFILE { profile }

  alt profileCommitted && sshKeysGenerated
    note over C : show DeviceEnrollDialog\n(→ enrollment flow from T10)
  else !profileCommitted
    note over C : show ProfileEditor gate\n(→ commit flow from T8/T9)
  end
end

== Replay Protection ==

note over S #FFCCCC
  Challenge is single-use:
  • Stored in WebSocketClient on connect
  • Cleared after DEVICE_AUTH (success or fail)
  • New connection = new challenge
  • Replay of old challenge → rejected
end note

== Auth State Summary ==

note over S
  | authMethod | Meaning |
  | none | No auth attempted |
  | token | IDENTIFY only (legacy) |
  | device-key | Challenge-response verified |
end note

@enduml
